A||N||2||MikeSchaefer||Dimming Mirrors, what car should I get them from?||||5||
Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||03-05-2001||08:18 PM||||Hi, I'm going to the salvage yard on saturday and I would like to pick up one of those nice mirrors with the dimming feature built in.  Possibly the temp or compass feature too.  I have heard that some SUV's have these.  Well the yard requires me to know the vehicle's year and model when i request it, it isn't a pick and pull deal.  Can anyone reccomend a car to get a really nice mirror from for me please?<BR>Thanks a million,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||deceler8||03-05-2001||09:04 PM||||Obviously your best bet are the late model luxury cars (Caddy, Lincoln, etc...).<P>About all I know about these mirrors is that they're made by a company called Gentex. It's possible the Gentex web site lists which makes the mirrors are installed in.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bill Osmer||03-07-2001||12:52 PM||||As was stated, most late model luxury cars, and some SUVs will have them. I've installed them in my Fiero, and love 'em. They usually come with 3 wires, only need to connect 2 of them (batt & grnd). You'll have to run a switched (ign) wire to the mirrors to power them , or they'll be on all the time.<P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
